                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have played this series through most of it's incarnations. DDS: Pro Basketball 2017 is by far the best.\n\nIf you are interested in a basketball GM sim, in the vein of Baseball Mogul or OOTP Baseball, or are a fan of management games, this game is the best basketball game available. In previous versions it was difficult to build teams using the draft, this version while not perfect offers a realistic team building experience. Occasionally you will find the next LeBron James or Stephen Curry, but more often then not you do not. You have a wide variety of stats to sift through including advanced stats like TS% and +/- stats. Often times a player's rating does not reflect their actual impact on the game and in this case carefully tweaking the roster can result in your team winning more games. Overall it is an accurate simulation of being an NBA basketball GM.\n\nI have put hours into this game and similar versions and overall I highly recommend the game for people who are into this genre. It is a lot better than the previous versions as far as statistical accuracy.\n\nPROS:\n\nBest Basketball Management Game on the Market.\nFairly accurate stats.\nComputer generated players have relatively realistic statistics.\nTeam chemistry matters.\nYou can make expansion teams\nTons of stats to sift through\n\nCons\n\nYou can exploit CPU AI(To a degree, the CPU GMs are not complete idiots)\nToo many players play all 82 games\nThe D-League Draft takes too much time.\nDraft is a little too predictable, no random surprises in the 2nd round.\n\nOverall highly recommended. Much better than previous incarnations.\n",
